  "outcome_use": "descriptive_after_frozen_assignment_never_for_model_or_k_selection",
  "external_reproducibility_rule": "An internally stable MIMIC-IV solution is a local candidate phenotype structure only. It cannot be called transportable or generalizable without external-database reproducibility using the same frozen representation and assignment protocol.",
  "reportability_rule": "If minimum BIC occurs at the upper candidate boundary k=6, report no interior solution in the prespecified range. If an interior BIC-selected candidate violates the minimum cluster fraction or completed stability mean adjusted Rand index is below 0.70, the formal scientific result is no stable phenotype solution. A numerical/refit engine failure is an execution failure, not a scientific null. Do not try another k, seed, threshold, exclusion, feature set, or imputation rule after seeing the result.",
